# The vendored TradingView charting library is a third-party artifact that gets
# re-copied from the monorepo on every mirror refresh.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` pins it to LF in the repository and on checkout, so the diff
# does not depend on the refreshing machine's `core.autocrlf`. Without this, a
# refresh from a Windows checkout with autocrlf=true and one from a Linux box
# produce a spurious 1465-file diff against each other.
#
# `text=auto` (not a bare `text`) is deliberate: it lets git keep detecting the
# binary assets — the fonts and images — and leave their bytes untouched. Forcing
# `text` here would corrupt them.
public/static/charting_library/** text=auto eol=lf
